a group of pro-democracy activists in  hong kong have been sentenced for taking  part in  anti-government protests in 2019 veteran  campaigner martin lee  who helped launch the city's largest  opposition party in the 1990s was given  a suspended sentence  of 11 months but media tycoon jimmy lai  received a 12-month jail term the 2019  protests were spurred  by beijing's tightening of freedoms in  hong kong  we can go live now to adrian brown he  joins us from hong kong outside the  courthouse  you were there for those hearings adrian  what more can you tell us  well yes jimmy lye has received as you  say a 12-month sentence that sentence  will now begin on friday  significantly additionally on friday two  new charges  were laid against jimmy lie including  another one  under the draconian national security  law that means that jimmy lye  is now facing three charges under the  national security law  in addition to another charge and  remember  there's been a campaign in mainland  china  for jimmy lai to stand trial there so  the fact he's now facing three charges  under the national security legislation  may make it easier  for that possibly to happen now jimmy  lie  as you say has received a 12-month  sentence the judge took into  account various mitigating factors the  fact that jimmy ly's health  is not good the fact he had no previous  convictions  but she also said that a deterrent  sentence was necessary she said the  activists knew full well that they were  defying the police  by taking part in that unauthorized  protest on august the 18th 2019  this was a protest that drew according  to the organizers  1.7 million people and that was a time  when emotions really were very high in  hong kong  and the magistrate argued that you know  it was possible that demonstration  which was peaceful could well have  become violent  martin lee as you mentioned the father  of democracy here in hong kong who  helped to co-author the basic law hong  kong's mini-constitution  received an 11-month sentence that's  been suspended for  two years a mitigating factor in his  case  is the fact that he is 82 years old so  we have  four people who have received suspended  sentences  and five others who have been jailed for  terms between  eight months and 18 months  thank you very much indeed adrian brown  there reporting live  from hong kong
 

